const CH13: CompactQuestion[] = [
  // Ch 13: The Value of Work (20 MCQs)
  [1, 1, 'In economics and everyday life, distinguish simply between **Economic Activities** and **Non-Economic Activities**:', 'Economic activities involve gardening only; non-economic means driving cars', '**Economic activities** are performed to earn income/livelihood (wages, salaries, shop profits, fees); **Non-economic activities** are performed purely out of love, care, gratitude, or civic duty WITHOUT monetary payment (like parents cooking home dinners or helping neighbours)!', 'Non-economic means illegal stealing', 'Economic means zero payment forever', 'B', 'Money changes how economists track GDP—yet non-economic care makes life deeply meaningful!', 'factual'],
  [1, 1, 'Give ONE clear example each of an Economic Activity and a Non-Economic Activity involving **teaching** or **cooking**:', 'Both always require hotel bills', 'A restaurant chef/paid school teacher earns regular salary/fees (Economic); a father cooking warm Sunday lunch for his family or an older sister helping her brother revise math free of charge (Non-economic)!', 'Home cooking earns hourly tips', 'School teachers never draw salaries', 'B', 'The exact same physical skill shifts category depending purely on monetary exchange intent!', 'application'],
  [1, 2, 'List three distinct forms in which people receive monetary compensation (**income/remuneration**) for Economic work:', 'Smiles, applause, and handshakes', '**Wages** (daily/hourly pay e.g. farmhand/mason), **Salaries** (fixed monthly employee pay e.g. nurse/teacher), and **Fees/Profits** (independent doctor/shopkeeper/plumber)', 'Rainwater, leaves, and sand', 'Borrowed toys only', 'B', 'Recognizing varied pay structures demystifies everyday careers cleanly.', 'factual'],
  [1, 2, 'What is **Payment in Kind** (compared to cash/bank salary) occasionally seen in rural harvests or apprenticeships?', 'Paying exclusively in foreign gold bars', 'Compensating work cleanly with valuable goods/produce (e.g., bags of harvested mangoes, sacks of wheat, free housing/meals) instead of currency cash!', 'Refusing to pay workers anything', 'Using imaginary monopoly notes', 'B', 'Non-cash tangible compensation complements monetary wages historically and locally.', 'factual'],
  [2, 1, 'Explain why **Value Addition** (turning cheap raw timber or raw flour into refined furniture or warm pastries) increases economic value:', 'Factories paint wood white secretly', 'Applying human craft, tools, design, electricity, and skill transforms plain raw material into far more useful durable finished products worth higher prices!', 'Timber gets heavier when cut', 'Flour tastes sour raw', 'B', 'Skilled labour transforms raw commodities into high-value goods.', 'conceptual'],
  [2, 1, 'Look at traditional Indian **Seva** (selfless volunteer service) such as cooking free meals at **Gurudwara Langars**, village **Van Mahotsav** tree planting, or disaster rescues: Why is such non-economic work priceless despite earning Rs 0 wage?', 'It wastes community hours', 'Selfless community *seva* weaves trust, feeds hungry strangers with dignity, heals forests, and fosters shared citizenship impossible to purchase purely with coins!', 'Only idle unemployed folks volunteer', 'Volunteering ruins shop sales', 'B', 'Non-monetary *seva* generates immense social wealth invisible in bank ledgers.', 'conceptual'],
  [2, 2, 'Why does society rightly recognize caring unpaid **homemaking work** (cooking nutritious meals, nursing sick toddlers/elders, organizing households) as extraordinarily valuable even though it rarely shows up in national GDP salaries?', 'Mothers and fathers work 15 minutes weekly', 'Without tireless unpaid domestic care, nobody could rest healthily, attend school focused, or arrive energetically at paid factories and offices!', 'Paid work needs no meals', 'Domestic work uses zero skill', 'B', 'Unpaid care work silently underpins the entire paid economic engine!', 'conceptual'],
  [2, 2, 'Identify what **Dignity of Labour** truly means inside any fair school or democracy:', 'Only office air-conditioned jobs deserve respect', 'Every honest useful occupation—sweeping clean streets, plumbing leaking taps, farming wheat, coding, or performing surgery—deserves equal human respect without mocking manual work!', 'Manual workers shouldn’t speak up', 'Salary size measures human character', 'B', 'Honouring every honest skill dismantles arrogant social stigma.', 'factual'],
  [3, 1, 'Observe Geeta Aunty (an Air Force pilot/engineer) vs Rajesh Uncle (a helpful carpenter building school desks) vs Grandmother sewing festival clothes joyfully free for grandchildren: Classify these three accurately:', 'All three are non-economic hobbies', 'Pilot & Carpenter perform skilled **Economic** livelihood work; Grandmother sewing lovingly free for grandkids performs priceless **Non-economic** care!', 'Pilot is non-economic; carpenter is unpaid', 'None add value to society', 'B', 'Testing real-life scenarios clarifies intent vs social value cleanly.', 'application'],
  [3, 1, 'When Anu’s neighbourhood cleans clogged community flowerbeds together every 1st Sunday (**Swachh Bharat / Civic Seva**), what double reward blooms even with zero wages?', 'Pocket gold coins appear underground', 'Cleaner healthier greenery for all children to play safely PLUS warm neighbourhood solidarity!', 'Municipal taxes triple automatically', 'Bugs vanish from Earth', 'B', 'Collective non-economic stewardship lifts community life quality directly.', 'conceptual'],
  [3, 2, 'Explain how an identical carpenter building desks at school (Economic) vs repairing his elderly widowed neighbour’s crooked broken cot completely free on Sunday (Non-Economic) illustrates shifting motive:', 'Skills vanish on Sundays', 'The exact identical woodworking expertise functions as paid livelihood during work hours and generous *seva* during community service!', 'Cots require no wood', 'Carpenters lose tools free', 'B', 'Purpose and exchange context—not manual complexity—define economic vs non-economic classification.', 'conceptual'],
  [3, 2, 'Notice how **Swachh Bharat Abhiyan** and **Van Mahotsav** rely heavily on student & citizen participation alongside salaried sanitation crews. Why?', 'To fire all workers immediately', 'Even spotless paid maintenance collapses if citizens litter recklessly—shared voluntary care fosters respect for sanitation workers AND pride in clean streets!', 'To avoid sweeping forever', 'Trees grow exclusively on paper', 'B', 'Shared participation builds empathy for essential municipal crews.', 'application'],
  [4, 1, 'Why can over-focusing ONLY on "highest salary numbers" while mocking sanitation crews, farmers, tailors, or caregivers destabilize an economy?', 'Everyone becomes a plumber overnight', 'Imagine any city if cleaners, farmers, electricians, and bus drivers stopped working for even 4 days—high-paid offices would halt immediately! All honest skilled work forms one interdependent web!', 'Farmers earn billions easily', 'Cities survive on laptops without food', 'B', 'Essential physical services carry colossal social indispensable value regardless of paycheck disparity.', 'conceptual'],
  [4, 1, 'Identify the FALSE statement regarding "The Value of Work":', 'Salary is regular monthly pay, whereas daily-wage earnings vary with hours or days worked', 'Community *Langars* and free tree-planting drives exemplify non-economic community *seva*', 'Only tasks paid in paper money hold real value to human happiness, health, or national progress', 'Adding human design and skill turns cheap raw ingredients into higher-value products', 'C', 'Unpaid family care, mentorship, and selfless volunteering hold monumental real human worth!', 'conceptual'],
  [4, 2, 'Compare **Intrinsic Satisfaction** vs **Financial Wage**: Can paid economic work ALSO bring deep personal joy and pride?', 'No—wages poison enjoyment automatically', 'Yes! A dedicated village teacher, potter, doctor, or baker earns an honest living (Economic) while caring passionately for pupils’ smiles or fine craft quality!', 'Paid workers hate every morning', 'Only millionaires enjoy music', 'B', 'Purposeful mastery aligns livelihood cleanly with personal dignity.', 'conceptual'],
  [4, 2, 'Which famous Indian leader famously cleaned toilets and spun cotton yarn daily inside his ashram specifically to smash arrogant prejudice against manual labour?', 'Lord Curzon', 'Mahatma Gandhi (alongside saints like Kabir and Guru Nanak who dignified honest manual labour!)', 'Aurangzeb', 'Lord Dalhousie', 'B', 'Gandhiji’s insistence on shared ashram sanitation upheld *Dignity of Labour* unconditionally.', 'factual'],
  [5, 1, 'Assertion (A): Even though parents’ loving care for sick children or homework mentorship generates zero tax receipts, no sane nation treats family care as "worthless." Reason (R): Unpaid non-economic family care nurtures physical health, emotional security, and moral curiosity—building the capable adults who power society!', 'Both A and R are true, and R explains A', 'Both A and R are true, but R does not explain A', 'A is true, R is false', 'A is false, R is true', 'A', 'Distinguishing market GDP accounting from genuine human value shows deep economic maturity.', 'assertion-reason'],
  [5, 1, 'Assertion (A): Mocking skilled trades like tailoring, carpentry, or farming while chasing only desk titles shows genuine educational superiority. Reason (R): Mastering precision hands-on craft and honoring **Dignity of Labour** enriches sustainable communities and individual self-reliance equally alongside academic professions.', 'Both A and R are true', 'A is true, R is false', 'A is false, R is true', 'Both A and R are false', 'C', 'Disrespecting manual labour reflects prejudice, never intelligence.', 'assertion-reason'],
  [5, 2, 'Case Study: While helping organize a classroom "Career & Service Fair," some students want to invite ONLY doctors and software engineers, leaving out local bicycle mechanics, organic vegetable farmers, and school bus drivers! Using "The Value of Work," how should the teacher broaden their invitation list?', 'Drop the fair completely', 'Celebrate BOTH paid skilled professions (farmer, mechanic, bus driver, doctor, engineer—all vital economic contributors!) AND unpaid community caregivers (parent volunteers, animal rescuers) equally on one honour wall!', 'Pay students to attend', 'Invite zero parents', 'B', 'Inclusive representation models *Dignity of Labour* memorably in school life.', 'case-based'],
  [5, 2, 'Case Study: A young baker buys local organic wheat flour, pure jaggery, and almonds for ₹120, bakes crisp artisan millet cookies using skilful baking care, and sells the fresh box cleanly at the fair for ₹250. Which economic concept explains the ₹130 gain accurately?', 'Stealing coins from jars', '**Value Addition**—applying human labour, skill, oven energy, packaging, and clean hygiene converted raw ingredients into a convenient ready-to-eat valued good!', 'Inflation magic alone', 'Non-economic charity', 'B', 'Linking personal baking directly to *Value Addition* anchors micro-economics clearly.', 'case-based'],
];

